Package: libulmblas0
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: ${blas:Provides}
Description: BLAS with micro kernels selected for the CPU at load time
 ulmBLAS implements all routines of the reference BLAS (Basic Linear
 Algebra Subprograms) for single, double, complex and double complex
 precision with the Fortran 77 and the C (CBLAS) interface.
 .
 On amd64 libulmblas.so.0 selects at load time the build of the
 kernels for the CPU (AVX-512, AVX2 and FMA, SSE3 or generic x86-64)
 and registers itself as an alternative for libblas.so.3; on arm64 it
 uses NEON kernels.

Package: libulmblas-dev
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends: libulmblas0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: BLAS with micro kernels selected for the CPU at load time (development files)
 ulmBLAS implements all routines of the reference BLAS (Basic Linear
 Algebra Subprograms) for single, double, complex and double complex
 precision with the Fortran 77 and the C (CBLAS) interface.
 .
 This package contains the link libulmblas.so, the header cblas.h and
 the pkg-config file ulmblas.pc.
